#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD0030 expect=violation domain=LB
#note "FLIPPED noViolation -> violation by Fix #331 (M3-D18 / M2-D24 bucket 1, owner ruling 2026-08-22): NonEmptyGuardInliner's bare-emptiness arm is RETIRED (Fix #330), so the machine-emitted var_exists guard this scenario used to pin no longer exists; absent = all-missing, empty(X) is TRUE on every row and the rule reports the defect on exactly the rows its other conjuncts select (1 here). If this goes SILENT again, a guard is being injected -- escalate, do not rewrite toward silence. History, before Fix #330: FRESH - the batch's DISCRIMINATING executed-vs-skipped guard-matrix pin. Requirements.Variables.All is [--STRESU] ONLY, so the gate passes and the rule EXECUTES on violating-shaped data (units given, no LBSTRESC column at all); the shipped machine guard var_exists(\"--STRESC\") is false -> silent. expect=noViolation asserts EXECUTED-and-silent, not skipped."
#expectViolationCount 1
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col LBSTRESU type=Char label="Standard Units"
---
S1 | LB | 001 | 1 | GLUC | mmol/L
